the main focus of today's council was  the exchange of views on the European  semester documents in particular  employment and social policy aspects of  the country specific recommendations  after active discussions an agreement  has been reached on this issue council  conclusions were supported on equal  income opportunities for women and men  closing the gender gap during the  meeting the council conclusions on the  implementation of the youth guarantee  were also adopted the Commission stands  ready to assist member states in  reforming their economies yesterday's a  European Commission's college decided to  set up a new service structural reform  support service and any member state not  only program countries will be able to  request technical assistance to help  them in the implementation of  growth-enhancing administrative and  structural reforms although and even  across the European Union the  implementation of the youth guarantee is  bearing fruit however for its more  successful implementation increased  efforts are needed on outreach in  particular to the most marginalized  young people the council agreed on a  general approach on medical devices and  on vitro diagnostic medical devices the  aim is to ensure patient safety quality  control and availability of innovations
 

